{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>וישב.</b> The Nagid [Samuel ben Hofni] says that אנָא absorbs the lamed, like אל נא, and he explains אל from the root הואיל. This is far-fetched. Rather, אנָא — אל נא תעשה ככה — and he explains אנָא as an entreaty or as an expression of acknowledgment, like זה וככה אנָא ד׳ כי אני עבדך (Psalms 116:16)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:55.604368209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}